      "date": "2026-05-09T14:05:30.000Z",
      "title": "DALBHARAT: Upcoming Results And Dividend Decision Will Shape Earnings Outlook And Forward P/E",
      "body": "Analysts have trimmed their price target on Dalmia Bharat slightly from ₹1,870 to about ₹1,860, citing updated assumptions that combine a lower revenue growth outlook with a higher profit margin profile and a modestly reduced forward P/E multiple. What's in the News Board meeting scheduled for Apr 28, 2026 to review and approve audited standalone and consolidated financial results for the quarter and year ended Mar 31, 2026 (Key Developments).",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": "https://simplywall.st/community/narratives/in/materials/nse-dalbharat/dalmia-bharat-shares/m711ckhw-aggressive-expansion-will-exacerbate-overcapacity-in-cement-markets/updates/10-analysts-have-trimmed-their-price-target-on-dalmia-bharat-sl",
      "raw_subtype": "narrative-update"
    },
    {
      "id": "0c263eb8-9457-4de6-9698-be7d1afa73c5",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-04-30T11:56:20.000Z",
      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings: EPS in line with expectations, revenues disappoint",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹60.78 (up from ₹36.42 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹150.3b (up 7.5% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹11.4b (up 67% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 7.6% (up from 4.9% in FY 2025). The increase in margin was driven by higher revenue. Revenue missed analyst estimates by 1.9%. Earnings per share (EPS) were mostly in line with analyst estimates. Revenue is forecast to grow 8.9% p.a. on average during the next 3 years, compared to a 1.4% decline forecast for the Basic Materials industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 2% per year whereas the company’s share price has fallen by 2% per year.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "e1d904ab-cfd7-4fe8-8c6e-44f666749cb9",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-04-29T11:32:55.000Z",
      "title": "Consensus EPS estimates fall by 16%",
      "body": "The consensus outlook for earnings per share (EPS) in fiscal year 2027 has deteriorated. 2027 revenue forecast decreased from ₹166.5b to ₹164.4b. EPS estimate also fell from ₹72.56 per share to ₹60.59 per share. Net income forecast to shrink 3.6% next year vs 10% growth forecast for Basic Materials industry in India . Consensus price target broadly unchanged at ₹2,285. Share price fell 2.2% to ₹1,950 over the past week.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "91c890e6-db00-4060-a379-68cfbf378610",
      "type": "narrative-update",
